 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by the `parse_datetime` function in `tracker/timeutil.py` defaulting date-only inputs to midnight (00:00:00Z) instead of end-of-day (23:59:59Z). The fix modifies the function to set the time to 23:59:59Z for date-only inputs, ensuring due dates are correctly interpreted as the end of the day in UTC.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/timeutil.py b/tracker/timeutil.py\nindex 49fe1ca..6cf5991 100644\n--- a/tracker/timeutil.py\n+++ b/tracker/timeutil.py\n@@ -45,7 +45,8 @@ def parse_datetime(value, field=\"due_at\"):\n     try:\n         if len(text) == 10:\n             day = datetime.strptime(text, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n-            return datetime.combine(day, time(0, 0, 0), tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n+            day = datetime.strptime(text, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n+            return datetime.combine(day, time(23, 59, 59), tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n         parsed = datetime.fromisoformat(text)\n     except ValueError as exc:\n         raise ValidationError(f\"{field} is not a valid date\", {field: \"invalid\"}) from exc\n",
